the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    Gesamtbewertung holds for *a case*.
    Modul 1 holds for *a case*.
    Modul 2 holds for *a case*.
    Gesamtbewertung is decided for *a case*.
    Gesamtbewertung would hold for *a case*; unknown.
    Modul 1 is decided for *a case*.
    Modul 2 is decided for *a case*.
    the answer to Modul 1 for *a case* is *a truth value*; scenario element.
    Modul 1 would hold for *a case*; unknown.
    the answer to Modul 2 for *a case* is *a truth value*; scenario element.
    Modul 2 would hold for *a case*; unknown.

the knowledge base r3_6_accept_delegated_custom_combiner includes:

the text of the_rulemap is at "sources/accept-delegated-custom-combiner.ruml".

% Status des ersten Kindes
Gesamtbewertung holds for a case if
    Gesamtbewertung is decided for the case
    and Modul 1 holds for the case.

Gesamtbewertung holds for a case if
    it is not the case that Gesamtbewertung is decided for the case
    and Gesamtbewertung would hold for the case.

Gesamtbewertung is decided for a case if
    Modul 1 is decided for the case
    and Modul 2 is decided for the case.

Modul 1 holds for a case if
    the answer to Modul 1 for the case is true.

% Until a person answers, RUML's answer is undefined: the leaf holds only on the assumption below.
Modul 1 holds for a case if
    it is not the case that the answer to Modul 1 for the case is a truth value
    and Modul 1 would hold for the case.

Modul 1 is decided for a case if
    the answer to Modul 1 for the case is a truth value.

Modul 2 holds for a case if
    the answer to Modul 2 for the case is true.

% Until a person answers, RUML's answer is undefined: the leaf holds only on the assumption below.
Modul 2 holds for a case if
    it is not the case that the answer to Modul 2 for the case is a truth value
    and Modul 2 would hold for the case.

Modul 2 is decided for a case if
    the answer to Modul 2 for the case is a truth value.

